      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory RTO Paperwork, Transit Marine Insurance &amp; Delivery Handover for Transportation Khadda Kushinagar Safe</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When arranging car transportation in Khadda Kushinagar, having the right paperwork on hand not only smooths the process but also protects your vehicle during transit. Below is a concise checklist of the essential documents you must prepare before you hit the road.</p>
<h3><strong>1. Self‑Attested RC Photocopy</strong></h3>
<p>The Registration Certificate (RC) is the legal identity of your vehicle. A self‑attested photocopy—signed by you and stamped by a Notary Public—serves as proof of ownership and is mandatory for any transport service. This document must be up‑to‑date and clearly display the vehicle’s chassis number, engine number, and registration details.</p>
<h3><strong>2. Current Pollution Under Control (PUC) Certificate</strong></h3>
<p>All vehicles in India must carry a valid PUC certificate to confirm compliance with emission norms. Transporters require a copy of the latest PUC, typically issued by the local RTO or authorized testing centers. Ensure the certificate is not older than 90 days from the date of departure.</p>
<h3><strong>3. Valid Insurance Certificate</strong></h3>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">While standard insurance covers basic risks, it is advisable to opt for a dedicated marine transit insurance policy that covers the vehicle during sea or river transport.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>This policy should be 100% declared‑value, meaning the insurer agrees to pay the full market value of the car in case of loss or damage.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>A copy of this insurance certificate must accompany the vehicle’s paperwork.</span></li></ul>
<h3><strong>4. IBA‑Approved Consignment Bilty</strong></h3>
<p>The International Bankers' Association (IBA) consignment bilty is the transport contract that governs the terms of shipment. It specifies pickup and delivery points, transit routes, and liability clauses. Transporters will require an IBA‑approved bilty signed by both the consignor and the carrier, confirming that all documents are in order before the vehicle is handed over.</p>
